<item>
  <title>Irrationality of Square Root</title>
  <link>https://stevenchen333.github.io/posts/Real Analysis/square_root.html</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<section id="motivation" class="level2" data-number="1">
<h2 data-number="1" class="anchored" data-anchor-id="motivation"><span class="header-section-number">1</span> Motivation</h2>
</section>
<section id="theorem-and-proof" class="level2" data-number="2">
<h2 data-number="2" class="anchored" data-anchor-id="theorem-and-proof"><span class="header-section-number">2</span> Theorem and Proof</h2>
<div id="thm-geometric-series" class="theorem">
<p><span class="theorem-title"><strong>Theorem 1 (Geometric Series)</strong></span> For any <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?r%20%5Cneq%201"> and positive integer <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?n">,</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Csum_%7Bk=0%7D%5E%7Bn-1%7D%20r%5Ek%0A=%0A%5Cfrac%7B1-r%5En%7D%7B1-r%7D.%0A"></p>
</div>
<div class="proof">
<p><span class="proof-title"><em>Proof</em>. </span>Let</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0AS%20=%201+r+r%5E2+%5Ccdots+r%5E%7Bn-1%7D.%0A"></p>
<p>Multiplying both sides by <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?r"> gives</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0ArS%20=%20r+r%5E2+%5Ccdots+r%5En.%0A"></p>
<p>Subtracting,</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A(1-r)S%20=%201-r%5En.%0A"></p>
<p>Since <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?r%5Cneq%201">, we obtain</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0AS%20=%20%5Cfrac%7B1-r%5En%7D%7B1-r%7D.%0A"></p>
<p>This completes the proof.</p>
</div>
<p>As established in Theorem&nbsp;1, the finite geometric series has a closed-form expression.</p>


</section>

